              absent, so the W7 test gate runs the headless TeslaSync.App.Tests project (the sibling-W7 convention).

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  SchemaDriftPage / ApiLogsPage do. The generated prompt's idealized "DLQInspectorPage.xaml +
  DLQInspectorPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped onto these real conventions; the surface
  registers with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("DLQInspector", already in RouteTable.cs → /admin/dlq).
- The page COMPOSES the four DLQ sub-surfaces that already exist (W3): StatusHeader, EntriesTable, AuditPanel
  (feature-views/, namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.DlqInspector) and the EntryDrawer side-sheet
  (modals-dialogs/, namespace TeslaSync.App.ModalsDialogs). The page owns the orchestration the web page owns:
  the selected row drives the drawer + the scoped useDLQEntry fetch; the pendingReplay row drives the confirm
  dialog; the replay outcome (or its 403) toggles the replay-blocked banner.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the four manifest data sources are the web hooks useDLQList / useDLQEntry / useDLQAudit /
  useDLQReplay. The view-model reads through four injected ports (IDlqListFeed / IDlqEntryFeed / IDlqAuditFeed /
  IDlqReplayService, DLQInspectorPage.Model.cs); the default Empty* feeds resolve the empty state (the
  SchemaDriftPage/ApiLogsPage host-injection precedent), and the generated-client-backed DlqListClientFeed /
  DlqEntryClientFeed / DlqAuditClientFeed / DlqReplayClientService (DLQInspectorPage.Source.cs) bind to the
  generated OpenAPI contract client operations get_api_v1_system_dlq / get_api_v1_system_dlq_id /
  get_api_v1_system_dlq_audit (+ _id_audit) / post_api_v1_system_dlq_id_replay, asserted against the generated
  endpoint table + the FakeApiClient in tests. No HTTP touches the view. A hard DLQ_REPLAY_ENABLED=false gate
  surfaces as ApiException StatusCode==403, mapped to the replay-blocked banner (web error.status === 403).
  The generated C# client (W1) is regenerated deterministically from api/openapi/teslasync.openapi.json via
  apps/tools/codegen/gen-clients.ts (it is git-ignored, not committed); Generated/Generated.csproj wraps it.
- The web page passes PageContainer only `query={list}` (not loading/error/empty), so the body always renders the
  children; the list data states surface per ADR-006 as visible Fluent regions: loading -> the page-tier
  TsDataFreshness chip (IsFetching → "Updating…") + the StatusHeader em-dash tiles + the EntriesTable/AuditPanel
  "Loading…" bodies; error -> the freshness chip (IsError → "Error") + a TsQueryError InfoBar + Retry; success ->
  populated tiles + the entries table + the audit table. Never a blank region.
- SI units N/A (this admin surface bears no unit fields — DLQ ids, topics, parse reasons, payload byte sizes and
  replay-audit rows only); counts/sizes/timestamps format through the shared NumberFormatting / DateTimeFormatting
  ports inside the composed sub-surfaces at the display boundary.
- All 10 i18n keys already exist verbatim (web key names) in Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw under the
  translation.* prefix (admin.dlq.pageTitle/subtitle/panels.entries/panels.audit/banners.replayBlockedTitle/
  banners.replayBlockedMessage/confirm.title/confirm.message/confirm.confirm + common.cancel); the surface resolves
  them through the ILocalizer facade with the web English defaults as fallbacks. confirm.message is stored with the
  positional {0} marker (the web {{id}} template); ConfirmMessage interpolates the pending entry id.

